{"symbol":"KWS.DE","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T18:24:39Z","info":{"address1":"Grimsehlstrasse 31","city":"Einbeck","zip":"37574","country":"Germany","phone":"49 5561 311 0","fax":"49 5561 311 322","website":"https://www.kws.com","industry":"Agricultural Inputs","industryKey":"agricultural-inputs","industryDisp":"Agricultural Inputs","sector":"Basic Materials","sectorKey":"basic-materials","sectorDisp":"Basic Materials","longBusinessSummary":"KWS SAAT SE & Co. KGaA breeds, produces, and distributes seeds for agriculture. It operates through Sugarbeet, Corn, Cereals, and Vegetables segments. The Corn segment breeds, produces, and distributes seed for corn and sunflowers. The Sugarbeet segment engages in breeding, production, and distribution of sugarbeet seeds, as well as the development of diploid hybrid potatoes. The Cereals segment breeds, produces, and distributes seeds for rye, wheat, barley, and oilseed rape. This segment also offers other crops, including peas, catch crops, and oats. The Vegetables segment engages in the breeding, production, and distribution of seeds for spinach, beans, Swiss chard, red beet, and tomatoes. The company was formerly known as KWS SAAT SE and changed its name to KWS SAAT SE & Co. KGaA in July 2019. KWS SAAT SE & Co. KGaA was founded in 1856 and is headquartered in Einbeck, Germany.","fullTimeEmployees":4552,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Felix  Büchting Ph.D.","age":51,"title":"CEO & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1974,"fiscalYear":2026,"totalPay":1335596,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Jorn  Andreas","age":45,"title":"CFO & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1980,"fiscalYear":2026,"totalPay":1233941,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Nicolas  Wielandt","age":45,"title":"Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1980,"fiscalYear":2026,"totalPay":1219230,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Sebastian  Talg","age":4